<title>DJIBOUTI: Dysentery kills nine children in Djibouti village.</title>
<headline>Dysentery kills nine children in Djibouti village.</headline>
<dateline>DJIBOUTI 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dysentery has killed nine children in a Djibouti village after a local well became polluted by a snake, national radio and television said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Around 100 residents of Goubetto, which stands on the Djibouti-Ethiopian railroad around 20 km (12 miles) southwest of the capital, have been treated for dysentery since mid-October when a snake reportedly fell into the well.</p>
</text>
